                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Custom Implementation</h3>
                            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                                <div><strong>Euler Method:</strong> O(h) first-order accuracy</div>
                                <div><strong>Implementation:</strong> Written from scratch to match the provided solvers</div>
                                <div><strong>Purpose:</strong> Baseline to compare the others against</div>
                                <div>
                                    <strong>Features:</strong>
                                    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-gray-400">
                                        <li>• Butcher tableau structure</li>
                                        <li>• Timed the same way as the other solvers</li>
                                        <li>• Type-safe</li>
                                        <li>• Light on memory</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Third-Order Methods</h3>
                            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                                <div><strong>SSPRK3:</strong> Strong stability preserving</div>
                                <div><strong>Van der Houwen:</strong> Optimized coefficients</div>
                                <div><strong>Accuracy:</strong> O(h³) convergence rate</div>
                                <div>
                                    <strong>Applications:</strong>
                                    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-gray-400">
                                        <li>• Simulations where stability matters most</li>
                                        <li>• Medium precision</li>
                                        <li>• A balance of speed and accuracy</li>
                                        <li>• Keeping oscillations intact</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Fourth-Order Methods</h3>
                            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                                <div><strong>Runge-Kutta:</strong> Classical RK4</div>
                                <div><strong>3/8-rule:</strong> Alternative RK4 variant</div>
                                <div><strong>Ralston-4:</strong> Tuned for stability</div>
                                <div>
                                    <strong>Performance:</strong>
                                    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-gray-400">
                                        <li>• O(h⁴) accuracy</li>
                                        <li>• Lowest errors of the group</li>
                                        <li>• The standard choice in practice</li>
                                        <li>• More work per step in exchange for accuracy</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Implementation Architecture -->
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Implementation Architecture</h3>
                        <div class="bg-ink rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-sm">
                            <div class="text-cy mb-2"># Custom Euler method following solver.py patterns</div>
                            <div class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
                                <span class="text-cy">def</span> <span class="text-cy">Eulers_Method</span>(rhs, y0, t0, dt, T):<br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text-cy"># Butcher tableau for Euler (1st order)</span><br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;matrix = np.array([[<span class="text-cy">0.0</span>]])<br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;weights = np.array([<span class="text-cy">1</span>])<br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;nodes = np.array([<span class="text-cy">0.0</span>])<br/><br/>

                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text-cy"># Time integration loop</span><br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text-cy">for</span> step <span class="text-cy">in</span> <span class="text-cy">range</span>(timesteps):<br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;k[i] = rhs(t_out[-<span class="text-cy">1</span>], y_out[-<span class="text-cy">1</span>])<br/>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;y_new = y_out[-<span class="text-cy">1</span>] + dt * k[<span class="text-cy">0</span>]
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </ProjectSection>

